open CategoryTheory

/-- **Auxiliary cyclic cyclotomic level with prescribed local degree (finite place).**

For a finite Galois extension `L/k` of number fields, a finite place `v₀` of `k` and `N > 0`, there
are fields with `k ⊆ M`, `k ⊆ L ⊆ E`, `M ⊆ E`, such that `M/k` is cyclic and cyclotomic of prime
conductor, `E` is generated by `L` and `M` over `k`, and the local degree `[M_W : k_{v₀}]` at every
place `W` of `M` above `v₀` is divisible by `N`. -/
def EB_AuxFinite (k L : Type) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field L] [NumberField L]
    [Algebra k L] [FiniteDimensional k L] [IsGalois k L]
    (v₀ : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k)) (N : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ (M E : Type) (_ : Field M) (_ : NumberField M) (_ : Field E) (_ : NumberField E)
    (_ : Algebra k M) (_ : Algebra k E) (_ : Algebra L E) (_ : Algebra M E)
    (_ : IsScalarTower k L E) (_ : IsScalarTower k M E)
    (_ : FiniteDimensional k M) (_ : FiniteDimensional k E)
    (_ : IsGalois k M) (_ : IsGalois k E) (_ : IsCyclic (M ≃ₐ[k] M)),
    (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range (algebraMap L E) ∪ Set.range (algebraMap M E)) = ⊤) ∧
    (∀ (W : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers M)),
      W.asIdeal.LiesOver v₀.asIdeal →
        W.asIdeal.ramificationIdx (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k) = 1 ∧
          N ∣ W.asIdeal.inertiaDeg (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k))

open CategoryTheory

/-- **Bridge: the stabiliser of a finite place is its decomposition group.**

For `k ⊆ K ⊆ E` finite Galois extensions of number fields and a finite place `ŵ` of `E`, the
stabiliser of the place `Place.ofFinite ŵ` in `Gal(E/K)` is the decomposition group of `ŵ` in the
sense of `Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.decompositionSubgroup`.

Both sides are `{σ | σ • ŵ = ŵ}`; the two actions (`Place.smulHeightOneSpectrum` and the commons
`placeSmul`) are identified by `NK.GlobalCFT.Inclusion.smulHeightOneSpectrum_eq_placeSmul` and
`Commons…decompositionSubgroup`'s `mem_decompositionSubgroup`. -/
def EB_StabEqDecomp (k K E : Type) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field E]
    [NumberField E] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k E] [Algebra K E] [IsScalarTower k K E]
    [FiniteDimensional k K] [FiniteDimensional K E] [FiniteDimensional k E]
    [IsGalois k K] [IsGalois k E] [IsGalois K E]
    (ŵ : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers E)) : Prop :=
  MulAction.stabilizer (E ≃ₐ[K] E)
      (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ) =
    Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.decompositionSubgroup (K := K) ŵ

/-- **The local class-formation data at a finite place, in the stabiliser world.**

Two outputs of local class field theory for the local extension `E_ŵ/K_W`, transported to the
stabiliser `Γ = Stab_{Gal(E/K)}(ŵ)` acting on `E_ŵˣ` (`NK.HassePrinciple.localUnitsRep`, whose
action is `NK.HassePrinciple.localAutHom`):

* `Nat.card (H²(Γ, E_ŵˣ)) = |Γ|` (the local fundamental class gives the lower bound, the solvable
  dévissage the upper bound);
* `H²(Γ, E_ŵˣ)` has an element of order `|Γ|` (the local fundamental class).

The transport goes through `EB_StabEqDecomp` and
`Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.decompositionSubgroupMulEquivLocalGalois` (which is the
`Gal(E_ŵ/K_W) ≅ Stab` isomorphism), together with
`Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.groupCohomology_two_units_ge_finrank`,
`Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.natCard_groupCohomology_two_units_le_finrank_of_solvable`,
`Commons.NumberTheory.NumberField.Completion.exists_addOrderOf_eq_finrank_groupCohomology_two_units`
and the transport of representations along a group isomorphism
(`NK.NUV2.LC.nonempty_addEquiv_groupCohomology_res_mulEquiv`). -/
def EB_LocCard (k K E : Type) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field E]
    [NumberField E] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k E] [Algebra K E] [IsScalarTower k K E]
    [FiniteDimensional k K] [FiniteDimensional K E] [FiniteDimensional k E]
    [IsGalois k K] [IsGalois k E] [IsGalois K E]
    (ŵ : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers E)) : Prop :=
  Nat.card (groupCohomology (NK.HassePrinciple.localUnitsRep K E
      (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ)) 2) =
    Nat.card (MulAction.stabilizer (E ≃ₐ[K] E) (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ)) ∧
  ∃ u : groupCohomology (NK.HassePrinciple.localUnitsRep K E
      (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ)) 2,
    addOrderOf u = Nat.card (groupCohomology (NK.HassePrinciple.localUnitsRep K E
      (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ)) 2)


/-- **The local degree step of `brauer_single_place`.**

In the tower `k ⊆ L`, `k ⊆ M`, `k ⊆ E` of number fields with `L/k`, `M/k`, `E/k` Galois and
`E = L·M`, let `v₀` be a finite place of `k`.  Suppose that

* `M/k` is unramified at every place `W` above `v₀` and `N ∣ f(W|v₀)`, and
* the local degree of `L` at every place `r` above `v₀` divides `N`.

Then for every place `ŵ` of `E` above `v₀` and every class `a ∈ H²(Gal(L/k), Lˣ)`, the restriction
(along `Gal(E/k) → Gal(E/M)`) of its inflation to `E` is locally trivial at `ŵ`.

Mathematically: `res_{E/M}(inf_E a)` is the class `a ⊗_k M` over `M`; at `ŵ` its localisation is
`a ⊗_k M_W` in `Br(M_W)`, where `M_W/k_{v₀}` is unramified of degree `f(W|v₀)`; since `a`'s local
class at `v₀` lies in `Br(L_r/k_{v₀})` of order dividing `[L_r:k_{v₀}] = e·f`, which divides
`N ∣ f(W|v₀)`, and the unramified extension of degree `n` splits every class of order dividing `n`,
the localisation vanishes. -/
def EB_Crux (k L M E : Type) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field L] [NumberField L] [Field M]
    [NumberField M] [Field E] [NumberField E] [Algebra k L] [Algebra k M] [Algebra k E]
    [Algebra L E] [Algebra M E] [IsScalarTower k L E] [IsScalarTower k M E]
    [FiniteDimensional k L] [FiniteDimensional k M] [FiniteDimensional k E]
    [IsGalois k L] [IsGalois k M] [IsGalois k E] [FiniteDimensional M E] [IsGalois M E]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range (algebraMap L E) ∪ Set.range (algebraMap M E)) = ⊤)
    (v₀ : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k)) (N : ℕ) : Prop :=
  (∀ (W : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers M)),
      W.asIdeal.LiesOver v₀.asIdeal →
        W.asIdeal.ramificationIdx (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k) = 1 ∧
          N ∣ W.asIdeal.inertiaDeg (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k)) →
  (∀ (r : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers L)),
      r.asIdeal.LiesOver v₀.asIdeal →
        r.asIdeal.ramificationIdx (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k) *
          r.asIdeal.inertiaDeg (NumberField.RingOfIntegers k) ∣ N) →
  ∀ (ŵ : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers E)),
    ŵ.asIdeal.LiesOver v₀.asIdeal →
    ∀ a : groupCohomology (NK.HassePrinciple.unitsRep k L) 2,
      (NK.HassePrinciple.locUnits M E (NK.GlobalCFT.Place.ofFinite ŵ)).hom
        ((NK.NUV2.ChebAux.Transfer.resToGal k M E).hom
          ((NK.NUV2.ARL.HR.inflation (K := k) (L := L) (E := E)).hom a)) = 0

end Work.SSGRoute
